   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to accept an\napplication for a real property tax exemption from the Nassau Cemetery\nAssociation",
    "basePrintNo": "S9439",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9439-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9439\n\nSPONSOR: KAPLAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the county of Nassau assessor to\naccept an application for a real property tax exemption from the Nassau\nCemetery Association\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo allow the Nassau County Assessor to accept an application from the\nNassau Cemetery Association for a real property tax exemption.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Notwithstanding any other provision of law to the contrary,\nthe assessor of the county of Nassau is hereby authorized to accept from\nthe Nassau Cemetery Association an application for exemption from real\nproperty taxes. If accepted, the application shall be reviewed as if it\nhad been received on or before the taxable status date established for\nsuch roll.\n\nIf satisfied that such organization would otherwise be entitled to such\nexemption if such organization had filed an application for exemption by\nthe appropriate taxable status date, the assessor, upon approval by the\nNassau county legislature, may make appropriate correction to the\nsubject rolls. If such exemption is granted and such organization,\ntherefore, shall have paid any tax with respect to the subject rolls,\nthe applicable governing body or tax department may, in its sole\ndiscretion, provide for the refund of those taxes paid and cancel those\ntaxes, fines, penalties, liens or interest remaining unpaid.\n\n§ 2. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Nassau Cemetery Association purchased this piece of property on June\n24, 2021, with the deed recorded on July 8, 2021. An application was\nmade for the property to be exempt from taxation for real property taxes\nand was approved for the 2022/2023 school year and the 2023 year general\nassessment roll. This legislation retroactively allows that exemption to\nbe offered for the preceding year.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
